---

The FLAC decoder core (`kryx-flac`) is an independent, clean-room
implementation of the FLAC format from its public specification. It contains
NO third-party codec code: no libFLAC, no vendored C, no decoder crates.
The core crate has zero runtime dependencies.

Build- and binding-only dependencies (not FLAC code):

Rust crates:
  - napi (MIT)         — Node.js binding, flac-node only
  - napi-derive (MIT)  — Node.js binding, flac-node only
  - napi-build (MIT)   — build script, flac-node only

Node.js packages (devDependencies only — not shipped):
  - @napi-rs/cli (MIT)
  - vitest (MIT)
  - tsup (MIT)
  - typescript (Apache-2.0)
  - @biomejs/biome (MIT / Apache-2.0)
  - cross-env (MIT)

Full license texts of these dependencies are available in their
respective package distributions.
